{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/592351-imbued-hunters-a-different-take","id":592351,"title":"Imbued Hunters - A Different Take","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-15T23:21:22-07:00","id":592351,"title":"Imbued Hunters - A Different Take","content":"They're called the Imbued.<br /> <br /> Hunters, one and all of them. Men, women, and lord almighty, sometimes even children. They're a lot like us regular folk. They saw something that drew a flame in their heart. A mystery, an evil, an unknown. They didn't turn away. They acted, like we act. Together as one. Just is that they got some other kind of union going on. A deeper connection some have said. An almighty power above. That's horse shit.<br /> <br /> They just remember.<br /> <br /> See, it ain't some God or Principal, or Jesus they're seeing when they had their special moment. Naw. It was death. Always death. Many, many fucking deaths.<br /> <br /> Okay sure, lets get to the point. So what imbues em' eh? Gives em' those strength, those unreal powers?<br /> <br /> It's us. People. Hunters though really. What they remember in their Imbuing is the past. Lives of people, regular folks like us. Our struggles, our discoveries, our loves and our sins. They get hit with all of that in one single breath. An utterance of a connection deeper than flesh, deeper than blood.<br /> <br /> It's why bloodsuckers and witches can't put the whammy on them sometimes, when they draw on that connection their connected to that whole damn unified consciousness for strength, for guidance or for aid. You can will your demons to take hold of a single persons mind, a single persons soul. Add em' together though. You ain't got a snowballs chance in hell of swaying them.<br /> <br /> We've all tinkered with some mumbo jumbo at some moments. Magic, rituals, sacrifices, faith and holy texts. Some of us are better at it than others. Got the knack you could say.<br /> <br /> Well. That's how they got their unreal powers. They ain't so unreal. Most are just forgotten. We might have had them once. Priests, or wizards, demi-gods and heroes. Gone from this modern era, forgotten too, but not lost. They've lived on in these Hunters, these Imbued. Hell, it's not always ancient either, sometimes its just knowing how to drive a motorcycle like a badass or enchant a dagger to cut a ghost. I've done both, granted, never at the same time.<br /> <br /> Anyway. What does it mean to be one? Insanity. Complete and utter insanity. They have a connection to so much loss, so much rage, it can drive them mad and tear them apart. Vengeance doesn't even come close to describing the kind of lengths or appetites some will go to. But that's how you stop them. It's how the monsters keep them down.<br /> <br /> They're mortal, flesh and blood like us, but their gifts, their connection, it scares the hell out of the ghoulies and the mystagogues. They can read secret languages, codes never shared, riddles unknown. Tear down magical defenses, make their foes weep blood tears flavored with each of the sins they've committed. They're hell on ice, and scary boogeymen for sure. But theres a point where that all ends.<br /> <br /> See, they're Imbued with this connection because something in them connects them to us, a common humanity, a call against the monsters of the night, against evil, terror and fear no matter in what place it dwells, be it the hearts of mortals or creatures beyond. Their exploits are guaranteed to continue on, their lives embedded and imbued into the next Hunter. That's why the monsters terrorize them so. Not just because they probably want some sweet payback, but because they want to drive the next sucker crazy, so crazy they can't do what they're suppose to really do.<br /> <br /> Help save people. From the other, from themselves, from suffering, deliver us from evil and all that razzamatazz.<br /> <br /> That's why the connection gets severed when they go too dark, too deep. To help protect what they are. A living will and testament against the dark. Proof we aren't cattle, proof we can contend with what's out there in the night, proof that you can't kill hope.<br /> <br /> The ones off the reservation. They still keep what they've learned from those past lives. Still know the old powers and magics. Still are a pain in the butt to put down. They've become a monster, and I'll be damned if I haven't seen the next Imbued stare them right in the face in horror as they saw what they have become.<br /> <br /> Nope. They've got a shittier job than us. They don't get to buy the farm. They live on. They endure. They remember us, because when they made their choice between being an individual and sacrificing their unique soul to join the ranks, they did so with the hope that a difference could be made.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's what the Imbued are son, that's what you've just become. I know its scary and the dreams don't make sense, but they will soon enough. You'll understand just what kind of a crazy fucked up world of darkness we live in and then you'll do something about it. It's who you are, and who you've always been before.<br /> <br /> I'm proud of you, and I'm sorry for having to leave ya early but see, I've lost a lot of blood, and I, well. I miss your mother terribly. I can still picture her face, and her smile.<br /> <br /> I'm rambling kid, you get, go on. Learn from them. Those people who died before you. Who suffered and lost. Learn and win or hell, give it your best shot for the next guy right?<br /> <br /> Heh. It's all fuzzy here kid, I can almost see... her... smiling back at.... me...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","user":"GilboD","date":". 07-16-2015, 02:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T08:18:34-07:00","id":592641,"title":"","content":"Some questions for all you Hunter: The Vigil and Hunter: The Reckoning fans.<ul><li>Would you like to see Imbued become some kind of Splat or Conspiracy or Mystery Cult if they came back with this fiction supporting them?</li> </ul><ul><li>Do you prefer the idea of the Messengers or does it strike a more resonant chord that these Imbued Hunters are connecting with past lives, not their lives to be sure, but the lives of Hunters?</li> </ul><ul><li>If you do like my take on things, do you think they could work mechanically and be balanced for a second edition of Hunter?</li> </ul><ul><li>Is their anything you would add, subtract or change to this new take to make it cooler, better, more in theme with a second edition of Hunter?</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T10:00:31-07:00","id":592853,"title":"","content":"I think such Imbued would be a fine addition to the game. I mean, people who are forced by a higher power to take up the fight against the dark are a perfectly solid concept. The problems with Hunter: the Reckoning lay elsewhere, and wouldn't apply if the Imbued were a group in addition to all the other mortals who fight the denizens of the crowded shadows of the World of Darkness. I think that connecting with humanity's collective will to fight is a better fit for Vigil than Messengers were, too. The problem with Messengers was that it basically rendered mortals helpless sheep without some otherworldly angels stepping in and uploading powers into their brains. That's not what people want from a Hunter game.<br /> <br /> As for balancing them... hm. I think such hunters would work better as a minor splat rather than just a conspiracy, with a fuller set of powers than just an Endowment. But that's just me. Not sure about nWoD 2e, since we have no idea what changes a 2e Hunter game will bring, if it happens at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}